 a reviewer can answer “is this client financial-grade?” by reading one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field. The same philosophy as the rate-limit postures: ordinary clients see no behaviour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change at all, because ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"Self::Standard","isActive":true},{"text":" is the serde default and every row","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before schema v38 decodes to it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ClientProfile"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OAuth2ClientResponse/profile":{"abstract":[{"text":"X5.1 — the registered posture and mTLS credentials. Read-back matters: an operator","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"auditing which clients are financial-grade should be able to answer it from this"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"endpoint rather than from the database.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oauth2clientresponse\/profile","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OAuth2ClientResponse\/profile","title":"profile","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"profile","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClientProfile","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13ClientProfileO"}],"kind":"symbol"}}}